WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.068
-Welcome back, everyone.

00:00:02.068 --> 00:00:03.435
We are talking to the
one-and-only Daniel Craig!

00:00:03.435 --> 00:00:07.073
Now...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:07.073 --> 00:00:10.242
...to celebrate your
15 years as James Bond,

00:00:10.242 --> 00:00:12.778
I thought we could do a
speed round of your Bond films,

00:00:12.778 --> 00:00:14.247
and just give us
the first memory

00:00:14.247 --> 00:00:15.615
that comes to your mind, okay?

00:00:15.615 --> 00:00:17.917
It could be a long story.
It could be one word.

00:00:17.917 --> 00:00:20.086
Just something
that reminds you.

00:00:20.086 --> 00:00:21.587
Okay, let's start with this.
-Okay.

00:00:21.587 --> 00:00:23.289
-"Casino Royale."
-Cranes.

00:00:23.289 --> 00:00:25.825
-Yes!
-Yeah, jumping off cranes.

00:00:25.825 --> 00:00:28.894
-Yeah. That's exactly right.
-Yeah. Yeah, yeah. Yeah.

00:00:28.894 --> 00:00:30.062
-"Quantum of Solace."

00:00:30.062 --> 00:00:31.764
-A lot of problems.

00:00:31.764 --> 00:00:33.867
No, it was all good.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:33.867 --> 00:00:35.335
It was all fine.
It was all great.

00:00:35.335 --> 00:00:37.237
I think the
rooftop chase in Siena,

00:00:37.237 --> 00:00:38.404
which is at the beginning
of the movie,

00:00:38.404 --> 00:00:42.008
which was a lot of --
Before I started "Bond,"

00:00:42.008 --> 00:00:43.776
I had a genuine fear of heights.

00:00:43.776 --> 00:00:45.612
I mean, like, not great at all.

00:00:45.612 --> 00:00:48.581
And when I --
I don't anymore.

00:00:48.581 --> 00:00:49.782
-Wow!

00:00:49.782 --> 00:00:51.217
-But I had to get up there
and sort of, like,

00:00:51.217 --> 00:00:54.320
incrementally go higher and
higher and higher and higher,

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:55.654
and then, eventually,
I was sort of

00:00:55.654 --> 00:00:58.390
leaping out of windows,
you know, into moving buses.

00:00:58.390 --> 00:01:01.261
It was a little like, you
know, -- It was quite an arc.

00:01:01.261 --> 00:01:03.429
-Wow!

00:01:03.429 --> 00:01:05.798
-Yeah.
-Oh, "Skyfall."

00:01:05.798 --> 00:01:06.966
-Judi Dench.
I mean, it's easy.

00:01:06.966 --> 00:01:08.367
That's the sort of --
-Yes.

00:01:08.367 --> 00:01:11.537
-I mean, you know, the fact
that I got to work with her

00:01:11.537 --> 00:01:15.174
on three movies,
and she's one of the most

00:01:15.174 --> 00:01:18.578
glorious, delicious
human beings on planet Earth.

00:01:18.578 --> 00:01:19.612
-She is, right?
-Yeah.

00:01:19.612 --> 00:01:20.913
-She looks that way.
Yeah, yeah.

00:01:20.913 --> 00:01:22.982
-Yeah.
-And, also -- She does.

00:01:22.982 --> 00:01:24.384
Who doesn't love Judi Dench?

00:01:24.384 --> 00:01:26.286
But, also, I remember Adele

00:01:26.286 --> 00:01:28.221
doing the theme on this one.

00:01:28.221 --> 00:01:29.956
Adele. Come on.
-I mean, it's all -- Yeah.

00:01:29.956 --> 00:01:32.458
-Yeah, exactly.
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:01:32.458 --> 00:01:35.194
-"Spectre."

00:01:35.194 --> 00:01:39.265
-We did the biggest explosion
in movie history,

00:01:39.265 --> 00:01:40.633
out in the Moroccan desert.

00:01:40.633 --> 00:01:42.268
I don't know if we told
the Moroccan government

00:01:42.268 --> 00:01:46.839
that we were doing it,
but all I know is that

00:01:46.839 --> 00:01:49.142
Léa Seydoux and I
were standing there,

00:01:49.142 --> 00:01:52.145
and we basically --
They were on our back

00:01:52.145 --> 00:01:53.979
and they rolled the camera.

00:01:53.979 --> 00:01:55.915
And this thing
started blowing up,

00:01:55.915 --> 00:01:58.083
and I could feel Léa
just, like --

00:01:58.083 --> 00:02:00.319
just leaping further backwards,

00:02:00.319 --> 00:02:01.487
and I was just saying,
"Stay in shot, stay in shot.

00:02:01.487 --> 00:02:02.488
We can't do this again.

00:02:02.488 --> 00:02:03.857
We can't do this again."
-Wow!

00:02:03.857 --> 00:02:04.990
-I mean, it was terrifying.

00:02:04.990 --> 00:02:06.625
It was like, I mean,
this thing just rose up,

00:02:06.625 --> 00:02:09.528
and the percussion on
your face -- it was remarkable

00:02:09.528 --> 00:02:11.897
and kind of incredibly moving
in weird way.

00:02:11.897 --> 00:02:15.034
-Yeah.
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:02:15.034 --> 00:02:17.904
-"No Time to Die."

00:02:17.904 --> 00:02:21.874
-So many memories from that.

00:02:21.874 --> 00:02:22.908
I don't know.

00:02:22.908 --> 00:02:25.211
It's like the culmination
of all that.

00:02:25.211 --> 00:02:26.512
That's what I'd say.

00:02:26.512 --> 00:02:29.682
I mean, that just -- This exists
because of these four.

00:02:29.682 --> 00:02:33.686
-Yeah. I can't even begin
to thank you enough,

00:02:33.686 --> 00:02:36.689
as a fan, just of movies,
but also of James Bond,

00:02:36.689 --> 00:02:38.791
what you added to the character,

00:02:38.791 --> 00:02:41.527
the way you, like,
reinvigorated the franchise,

00:02:41.527 --> 00:02:43.362
the fact that
when you made him --

00:02:43.362 --> 00:02:45.398
You made him extra-human,
and I think

00:02:45.398 --> 00:02:48.400
this last one, people are gonna
flip for your performance.

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:51.171
I thought maybe --
-Can we have a drink now?

00:02:52.371 --> 00:02:55.073
-I had to.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:55.073 --> 00:02:57.777
I had to.
♪♪

00:02:57.777 --> 00:03:02.915
I'd be honored to share a cheers
to a martini with you.

00:03:02.915 --> 00:03:05.118
Mr. Bond, Mr. Craig,
thank you for everything.

00:03:05.118 --> 00:03:07.153
-Cheers to you.
-15 years.

00:03:07.153 --> 00:03:09.822
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:09.822 --> 00:03:10.957
-Wow. That's not bad.
-That's not that bad.

00:03:10.957 --> 00:03:12.291
-That's not bad.
-Daniel Craig.

00:03:12.291 --> 00:03:15.428
"No Time to Die" is in theaters
and IMAX right now.

00:03:15.428 --> 00:03:16.629
We'll be right back with
Meghan Trainor.

00:03:16.629 --> 00:03:17.730
Stick around.

